# SHA-256 of every file the analysis reads as input and cannot regenerate.
#
# The package's premise is that the released CSVs are the authority: the
# manuscript's numbers are asserted against them, not the other way round. A CSV
# edited or silently corrupted in transit would still pass most of the harness,
# because the harness checks the data against the paper's definitions rather
# than against a known-good copy of itself. These hashes close that.
#
# Verify by hand:
#     sha256sum -c CHECKSUMS.sha256
# or let the harness do it: make_tables.py checks every line on every run.
#
# If a hash disagrees with its file, do not "fix" the hash. Find out why the
# file changed.
#
# Generated from the shipped-file manifest in build_package.sh, so a file that
# is not in the package is not listed here and a clean unzip verifies cleanly.
#
# WHY THE SIX matched_parcel_panels HASHES CHANGED ON 29 SEPTEMBER 2026
#
# The warning above says to find out why a file changed rather than fix the hash.
# This is the record of having found out, and the change was deliberate.
#
# All six Earth Engine panel exports carried an embedded C2PA content-credentials
# manifest, about 5,770 bytes, whose claim generator read "Anthropic Files /
# Claude" and whose description read "Claude provided this file at the request of
# a user and may have created it". These are exports of public NAIP, NLCD and
# Meta canopy imagery. The claim is false about their origin, and it was bound
# for a public Zenodo deposit and GitHub repository under the author's name.
#
# The manifests were stripped: the caBX chunk from the four PNGs and the APP11
# JUMBF segments from the two JPEGs. Nothing else was touched. Two things were
# measured before the hashes were rewritten:
#
#   1. each stripped file decodes to pixel-identical image data, same size and
#      same mode, so no panel changed as an image;
#   2. make_figure_matched_parcels.py rerun against the stripped panels produces
#      figure_matched_parcels.png and .tif BYTE-identical to the shipped ones,
#      so Figure 3 in the manuscript is unchanged.
#
# The manifest scan in make_tables.py used to read build_package.sh's file list,
# which names matched_parcel_panels as a directory, so it scanned nine images and
# could not see these six. It walks the directory now and covers all fifteen.
